Personas are a settings section
===============================

The persona was a chip in the top bar, which is a strange place for a file: it sat beside the model
name as though who is speaking were a per-conversation control like which model answers. It is not —
it is a document on disk that defines the assistant, and the person who wants to change it goes
looking in settings.

There is a Personas section now, and it does everything the chip could do plus the thing the chip
never could:

* **the file and the folder**, as real paths read from the engine rather than reconstructed in the
  webview;
* **edit, save to the shelf, open the folder, use the shipped persona** — the same actions, in one
  place, with the shelf listed underneath as rows that switch or delete;
* **what it says** — the full text of the persona that is loaded, unsummarised, in a scrollable
  reading pane. A persona is markdown on your own disk; the point of it being a file is that it can be
  read, so the section shows it instead of describing where it lives. That is also what makes the
  shipped Nora readable without cloning the repository.

